                                                                        <div id="m_-4509913772158722550modnew3-text386989d0-1af6-4a86-8ab4-c0ba31ce2abf">
                                                                          <p>
                                                                            <br>
                                                                          </p>
                                                                          <p>Call for Code was a supporter of FAU College of Engineering &amp; Computer Science’s <strong>Responsible AI Hackathon</strong> that took place on their campus in Florida on 23–24 February. Pre-hackathon workshops had leading researchers and practitioners present on the challenges and opportunities in developing reliable AI systems. In addition to talks on responsible, transparent, and explainable AI, IBMer Dr. Fernando Koch introduced students to generative AI with IBM watsonx™ and the 2024 Call for Code Global Challenge. Hackathon participants tackled societal challenges with groundbreaking tech solutions, and the event ended with an awards ceremony highlighting the remarkable talent and problem-solving skills of all participants. </p>
                                                                          <p>
                                                                            <br>
                                                                          </p>
                                                                          <p>Universities around the world have brought Call for Code to their campuses. Learn more about how we can work with your university.</p>
